				{
					"Title": "Extreme rainfall",
					"Text1": "A 100-year rain event occurs statistically once every century. The highlighted areas on the model are the areas that are at risk of flooding in the event of extreme rain. In houses with basements, water can also enter via the pipe network. These flood risks are not visible in the model. When the municipality plans for new buildings, flood risks are taken into account and demands are made for various measures.\n\nIt could, for example, be about raising the ground level and foundation level when building new houses. But it is at least as important to ensure that large amounts of water have somewhere to go. One of the measures the municipality is working on is to create submerged surfaces in parks and natural areas.",
					"Text2": "",
					"Datasource": "",
					"Legend1": "extremaregn",
					"Legend2": "",
					"Default": true,
