				{
					"Title": "Sea level rise",
					"Text1": "The sea is rising globally and will continue to do so for a long time due to global warming. In Norrköping, we still have land rise after the last ice age (post-glacial rebound), but it is slowing down and we will start to see the effect of the rising sea levels. If the global warming is limited, the sea level will rise less.\n\nIn Norrköping, we have for a long time not allowed construction on areas that are too close to the sea. For certain developments, there is a requirement that the ground must first be raised before development can be permitted. In the long term, we will need to protect low-lying buildings. Right now, the municipality is investigating the possibility of building dikes along the edge of the sea in certain areas or building some kind of lock in Kvarsebo.",
